package skill

const AnalysisRuntimeComparisonTeaching = "For independent baseline/current captures, use comparison={baseline:{path,source_quote},current:{path,source_quote}}. Each local verbatim quote contains only its own original path; paths are not inferred from names or array order. For one literal interval requested jointly for both captures, put time_start/time_end and its verbatim source_quote on the containing runtime_artifact_scope_profile; leave both sides without endpoints and preserve their local path quotes. Otherwise add paired time_start/time_end only to each side with its own literal interval and include that interval in its local quote. Never mix a shared outer interval with side endpoints or time_windows, fabricate side quotes, invent endpoints or borrow the other side's window. Use requested_scope=explicit_time_window for either bounded form, otherwise unspecified. Only a separately declared whole-capture request may use full_artifact, with its own verbatim runtime_artifact_scope_profile.source_quote outside comparison. Preserve valid comparison members when repairing scope or quotes. A common numeric interval requests independent acquisition, not matching devices, aligned clocks, workloads, differences, completeness or causality."

// The schema and analyzer contract share the same single-/multi-source choice.
// Numeric range, source identity and completeness are separate authorities.
const AnalysisRuntimeArtifactScopeTeaching = "This profile records the CURRENT USER REQUEST'S artifact scope, never a model-authored trace_query or log-search window. " + AnalysisRuntimeIntentAvailabilityTeaching + " " + AnalysisRuntimeComparisonTeaching + " Without comparison, for one attached or referenced capture, use full_artifact when the user asks about the supplied artifact as a whole and gives no narrower boundary (for example 'this trace' / '这份 trace'); copy that phrase verbatim to source_quote. Use explicit_time_window only for exact user-stated bounds. " + AnalysisRuntimeWindowMembersTeaching + " Use bounded_selector for a narrower frame/span/event without exact user-stated time bounds; copy the selector phrase. For bounded_selector, omit time_start, time_end and time_windows; stray coordinates are ignored and never promote the selector to an explicit time window. Use unspecified when artifact range is unclear. Explorer-chosen local query windows do not narrow a full_artifact request or authorize whole-artifact counts or completeness claims."
